menuconfig PKG_USING_CAMERA_FRAMEWORK
    bool "Camera drivers"
    default n
    select RT_USING_SYSTEM_WORKQUEUE
    help
      Enable the camera framework package, including the handle layer, the
      sensor drivers and the data-bus backends.

      This is the SF-PKG entry point of the camera_framework package: the
      package is built only when this symbol is 'y' (see SConscript).

      The sensor model and the communication form are NOT selected here any
      more. They live in the SDK camera module menu:
      Board Peripherals -> Camera 1
      (customer/peripherals/camera/Kconfig). The module selects this symbol
      when BSP_USING_CAMERA1 is enabled and a model is chosen, and the package
      reads SENSOR_USING_* / CAMERA_USING_* from that module Kconfig.

if PKG_USING_CAMERA_FRAMEWORK

    config CAMERA_BOARD_HAS_MCLK
        bool
        default y if CAMERA_XCLK_ENABLE
        help
          The board declared that the MCU feeds the sensor MCLK. Internal
          read-only symbol: it exists so the backend does not have to poke at
          board symbols all over the place.

    config CAMERA_XCLK_REQUIRED
        bool
        default y if SENSOR_USING_OV2640 && !CAMERA_USING_ARDUCAM_FIFO
        default y if SENSOR_USING_GC032A
        default y if SENSOR_USING_BF30A2
        help
          The compiled-in sensor cannot run without a master clock. An OV2640
          behind an ArduCam FIFO module is the exception: the module drives the
          sensor from its own oscillator.

    rsource "software/Kconfig"

endif
